STRING 694
{
ICE: Up top, it's a good idea to have a lot of snowball launchers in the early stages of the game. Then when you get the money, you should put an Exploder up to the line to freeze most of the enemies. If used with Poison, an Exploder is really the only ice tower necessary, because of it's huge splash. Down at the bottom, making a maze of all ice towers is the most effective way to use it. Try to put an Exploder in the front of your maze to slow enemies before they enter.
}

STRING 695
{
FIRE: Fire is best used up top. It really isn't that effective anywhere else, with the exception of the Flame Staff and Incinerator. As those 2 towers are the 2 most expensive of Fire, it's not a good choice for the bottom to pick Fire as their first element. But as for the top, getting a Meteor Watcher as soon as possible is usually the best choice. Then move on to Blast Furnaces, and finally the Flame Staff. Stack all of these up to the front line. The Incinerator is good when dropped back a little to clean up your leaks.
}

STRING 696
{
EARTH: Earth is best used at the top, and the top only. You should start by building Terrain Protectors at the front line to bomb the enemies as they spawn. Then move onto Gaia's Box, and do the same. And just keep on moving up in towers as you get the money, and keep bombing the front line with them. If you have the money, you could start to form a maze, which will work wonders up top.
}

STRING 697
{
TECH: Tech is best used on the bottom. It's pretty bad on top throughout the entire game. On the bottom, start with a few arrow and sniper towers. Then just save up, and build a large amount of Ion Cannons, Cruise Missile Launchers, and Nuclear Missile Launchers. When these three towers are built together in the back of the map in large quantities, they will kill huge amounts of units. This is a truly devastating strategy when all three back players use it.
}

STRING 698
{
CRYSTAL: Crystal towers are high-end towers, but at an expensive cost. They could be used anywhere on the map, so here's a breakdown of the strategies. On the top, it's all about Blasters and Busters. You'll have to start off with a few Shooters, but once Blasters become affordable, start building them up on the front line. Do the same with Busters. You might want to drop a Fury back a little to pick off any leaks you have. For the rest of the map, you should go through all of the towers, with the possible exception of the Buster. Start by mazing with Shooters and Blasters. Then, when you get the money, place a Fury and/or Slower at the end of your maze to pick off leaks. Once you have a stable defense, start saving for the Dissolver, which is the best non-laser tower in the game.
}

STRING 699
{
POISON: Poison is best used in the middle and bottom areas of the map. It's not that good on top as a first choice, but as a second choice, when the first element was ice, poison proves extremely useful up top. On the bottom, the best strategy is to maze. When you get the money, build 2-3 Spires. Later in the game, a few Crawlers work very well at wearing down the enemies. Then of course there is the Gas Chamber, which I find goes best at the end of your maze. One or two Sludge Flingers or Grave Makers are good additions in the middle of the maze. Don't build too many of those, though. If an ally near you is ice, maze with them to make a deadly combo.
}

STRING 701
{
STONE: Stone is pretty effective no matter where it's used. It's a little less effective up top, however, because of the lack of range. I find that Stone is best used by Orange and Purple. All that is needed for these two positions is 7 or 8 towers. Start with all pebble towers, then replace them with all Rock Blasters, then all Projectors. Once you're done with that, build 1 or 2 Faery Mages, and also 1 or 2 Destroyers in the front of your towers so its range is used to its full ability. A Paralyzer is nice at the end of the game when combined with all of these towers. Once you have done this, continue a normal maze. As for the rest of the positions, mazing with all of the towers is suggested.
}

STRING 702
{
ELECTRICITY: Electric towers are good anywhere, but mostly in the middle and bottom areas of the map. You should start by mazing shock towers, then build 2 or 3 Storm Callers in your maze. Chain Lightning works extremely well earlier in the game- NOT on top, however. The Sparkler has a good ground attack, and it is one of the best air towers in the game. It's always a good idea to have 1 Thunder Rod at the very beginning of your maze. Then there's the Battery, which you could put anywhere in your maze- front, back, middle, it really doesn't matter. The Battery is the must have tower for Electricity.
}

